    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Jose Caballero** serving as our clear offensive anchor; his score of 80.26 is bolstered by a potent combination of a favorable park factor, a +13% dynamic platoon advantage against Lopez, and a prime #5 spot in the order. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-first philosophy with **Corbin Carroll** (73.68) and **James Wood** (71.33). **Corbin Carroll** enjoys a significant boost from his #2 spot in the lineup, while **James Wood** capitalizes on an aggressive #1 leadoff assignment and a favorable matchup against Canning. With our primary objective being the accumulation of stolen bases and efficient contact, these three represent our highest probability of delivering elite roto-category production today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Austin Riley**, whose 51.66 score narrowly missed the cut behind the reliable efficiency of **Josh Naylor** and the platoon upside of **Kyle Karros**. While **Austin Riley** carries power upside, the combination of facing Lodolo\u2019s 3.83 xERA and his inefficiency against elite holding pitchers\u2014which throttles his stolen base potential\u2014made him the odd man out in a crowded UTIL/3B rotation. We are monitoring the winds closely for **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**, as the projected wind-out at the stadium provides a marginal lift to their otherwise moderate projections, though both remain tethered by low-to-mid lineup positioning. As always, keep a sharp eye on the **Mickey Moniak** status; he remains sidelined, and we will avoid any risk with our bench depth until his IL stint concludes.",
